ws_s: 'New orders appear on the start page under “new/accept” – open and tap “Accept order”.|“Start repair”, then record working time, parts (also from stock) and external invoices in the case.|Parts missing: “Waiting for parts” – fleet management and dispatch are informed; then “Resume repair”.|Record work not done right away as open items; safety-relevant open items block completion.|Done: “To final inspection”. Technical release is always given by a person from fleet management.|Enter a date when accepting or later use “Set/move date” – More → “Workshop plan” shows all dates per day, passed dates and jobs without a date; you can set the date there directly (“Suggest” only fills in the field and reuses an existing date of the same vehicle; “Vehicle also planned on” shows dates that could be combined).', help_fleet_t: 'Fleet management: handling new reports', help_fleet_s: 'Open new reports and tap “Confirm receipt” – the reporter is informed.|Check the priority; for safety defects “Lock vehicle” (dispatch sees the lock immediately).|“Approve repair” and choose the workshop; reject only with a reason.|The management panel shows all open cases and fleet agent findings that need action.', help_release_t: 'Final inspection and release', help_release_s: 'Open cases in status “Final inspection” and tap “Perform inspection” (18 checkpoints).|Defects from the inspection automatically become follow-up orders.|“Release technically” lifts the lock; if there are problems, “Request rework”.|Open non-safety items stay visible and are reported by the agent.', help_dates_t: 'Inspection dates, odometer and data quality', help_dates_s: 'More → Inspection dates: overdue and upcoming HU/SP/UVV/tachograph, gap list, CSV and calendar export.|Enter dates only with evidence; “Done” keeps every completion in the history.|Odometer readings with reading date; deviations only with a reason (e.g. odometer replaced).|More → Data quality shows missing or contradictory master data.', help_dispo_